Papel e celulose — Heizir F. de Castro (@ic-usp-pulp: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_2MH0P1GEP4X9Y1GA7QSVVS2Q8A
Heizir Ferreira de Castro, Escola de Engenharia de Lorena, Universidade de São Paulo. Processos Químicos Industriais II, Papel e celulose, 2009. [Author/university full text](https://sistemas.eel.usp.br/docentes/arquivos/5840556/434/apostila4papelecelulose.pdf) · [Official teaching-material index](https://sistemas.eel.usp.br/docentes/visualizar.php?id=5840855).

Read the entire pulping, bleaching, chemical recovery and paper-production introduction. Work its reaction/flow explanations and compare them with the substantial courses, technical books and independent quantities assigned in this subject. A concise apostila provides a Portuguese introduction rather than the entire advanced literature or operating knowledge.

The author, individual PDF title/year, contents and university-hosted access were checked on 29 October 2026. These public teaching notes retain copyright and component rights; free access is not represented as a blanket open licence. Historical data and external references keep their dates. The notes, slides, images and example data remain external links.

